course: dictionary
lesson: 1172
title: Broccoli and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Broccoli is a green vegetable with a thick stalk and many small, tight buds on top that look like tiny trees. Those buds are flower buds, so when you eat broccoli you are eating a flower and a stem. Read the words around a word and they will tell you what it means.
explain: Context clues help with new words. Read this: «Carrots and beetroot are roots, celery and asparagus are stems, lettuce and spinach are leaves, broccoli and cauliflower are flowers, and peas and beans are seeds.» Each group names one plant part, so broccoli must belong with flowers.
explain: A floret is one small piece of the broccoli head. Broccoli does not count like apples do, so you say «some broccoli», not «three broccolis». Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Eat your broccoli» still makes sense when broccoli means the green vegetable.
fact: Broccoli is a green vegetable with a thick stalk and tight flower buds on top.
fact: A floret is one small piece of the broccoli head.
fact: Broccoli is uncountable, so you say «some broccoli», not «two broccolis».
fact: In science, the parts of broccoli we eat are flower buds and stem.
fact: Broccoli, cauliflower, kale and cabbage all come from one wild cabbage plant, and they are all the same species.
exercise: «Broccoli and cauliflower are flowers» in the list of plant parts. Which plant part does broccoli belong to? | Roots | Stems | Seeds | *Flowers
exercise: What is a floret? | Whole green vegetable with roots | *One small piece of the broccoli head | A green leaf of lettuce | The thick stalk of the plant
exercise: Broccoli is uncountable. Which phrase uses it correctly? | *Some broccoli | Two broccoli florets of broccolis | Many broccolis | Three broccolis
test: In science, which two parts of broccoli do we eat? | *Flower buds and stem | Seeds and petals | Leaves and roots | Roots and seeds
test: «From one wild cabbage plant, farmers bred cabbage, broccoli, cauliflower, kale and Brussels sprouts.» What do all these vegetables share? | They are all fruit | They all grow in the sea | They are all roots | *They are all the same species
exam: A girl does not like broccoli at first, but after a few small bites with cheese she likes it. What does this show? | Girls in Arizona never eat vegetables | *Tasting a food again can change how much you like it | Broccoli is always disgusting | Cheese is bad for children
